✅  What are Containers , how do they differ from VM?
 Containers are running instance of container image. It contains  binaries , libraries necessary to run an application. It virtualizes the OS , Shares the Host OS  kernel & it packages the application and its dependencies. Hence, They are light weight , bootup fast , sizes in mb , process level isolation , Uses less resource
  VM virtualizes the h/w, Runs a full guest OS on top of the hypervisor.  The images huge in size / heavier [ in Gbs] Slow to start , use lot of resources , It is h/w level isolation 
 

